; Aegis - the shielded bomber (GAMEPLAY-DESIGN P4.2, A2, A.q1-A.q3).
;
; hull 240 and speed 8 are the user's call of 2026-08-07, and the REASONING they
; gave is worth more than the numbers, because it generalises past this type:
;
;   "the less it can maneuver, the more hull it should carry. right? this can be
;    a great difficulty knob. I dont like bullet sponges, i admit, but a bomber
;    is exactly that, a big body that attracts damage and can also inflict large
;    damage with its ammunition."
;
; So durability is priced as the INVERSE of agility, and the sponge objection is
; answered by what the body is FOR rather than by trimming the number: an aegis
; you are grinding down is an aegis not delivering, which is the trade the type
; exists to offer. hull 80 -> 240 is the stated "at least 3 times tougher".
;
; speed 7 -> 8 is "ever so slightly faster" as asked, and it is deliberately a
; small move: 8 m/s is still the slowest thing in the roster by a wide margin
; (raider 14, falx 25, lance 34) and well under half a quad's cruise. Speed on
; this type attacks the CLOCK - how long you have between "it is here" and "it
; has released" - and the release is the interception deadline, so a large move
; here would be a much bigger change than it looks.
;
; THE SHIELD IS THE OTHER HALF, and it is behaviour rather than a number: as of
; 2026-08-07 every hit that arrives holds the screen down, on the shield or on
; the exposed hull, so the fight is exactly what the user described - break it
; with a missile, then STAY on it, and it rearms only if you lose contact for
; shield_regen_delay seconds. See health.gd; before that fix a 0.05-point sliver
; of regenerated shield made this body permanently immune to a blaster.
;
; NOTHING HERE IS BALANCED. Per H6 these are authored starting points; the
; harness measures the result and the hands decide the feel.

[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="EnemyConfig" load_steps=2 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://resources/enemy_config.gd" id="1_ecfg"]

